node_modules/
dist/
.DS_Store
*.log

# `public/models` is 1.1 GB of NASA public-domain meshes, fetched by a script in
# this repo rather than authored in it, and optional at runtime — the app falls
# back to compound placeholder hulls. The README documenting the expected file
# names is kept, and so is the generated catalogue, because
# `src/gfx/modelsManifest.js` is what the HUD selector reads.
public/models/*
!public/models/README.md

# `public/textures` is *not* ignored, and the 13 MB is deliberate.
#
# The obvious argument for fetching it instead is that a clone needs `npm
# install` anyway, so the network dependency comes free. That argument is wrong
# here: the two Moon maps arrive as TIFFs and are converted by `sips`, which
# ships with macOS and exists nowhere else. On Linux or Windows the fetch fails
# for exactly those two — 10 of the 13 MB — and does so *quietly*, because a
# failed source is skipped rather than fatal, leaving a photographed Earth beside
# a procedural Moon. Committing the converted output makes the imagery
# platform-independent and the repository genuinely self-contained.
public/draco/
